# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage
/blob-report/

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Playwright test artifacts
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Nightly-sync salvage drop (sync-bills.yml writes the un-pushed commit here
# when the commit step loses its race, for the upload-artifact step to collect).
# Runner-only; must never be committed by a stray `git add -A`.
salvage/

# scripts/check-journey-corpus.mjs's findings drop. On a runner it writes to
# $RUNNER_TEMP (the workflow reads the .md from there to file its issue); run
# by hand it falls back to the repo root, and neither file is ever an input to
# anything committed.
journey-corpus-report.json
journey-corpus-report.md
# scripts/check-scaffold-corpus.mjs writes its report the same way ($RUNNER_TEMP
# on a runner, the repo root by hand); one was committed by mistake on
# 2026-11-13 (#486).
scaffold-corpus-report.md

# Impeccable design-tooling state (owner decision 2026-08-02: critique
# snapshots ARE tracked — they carry the teardown campaign's trend lines —
# while machine-local state stays out of the tree)
.impeccable/hook.cache.json
.impeccable/config.local.json
.impeccable/design.json
.impeccable/live/

# scripts/gdelt-intake.mjs's circuit-breaker state (GDELT_STATE_PATH). Carried
# between runs by question-press.yml's Actions cache and never committed: that
# workflow's commit step stages data/question-press.json only, and this keeps
# a local run from ever staging it either.
.gdelt-state/

# The identical-bills step writes its file under a temporary name, then
# renames it; a kill in between must not put the temporary file in a commit.
/data/related-bills.json.tmp
# The short-titles step writes its three files the same way (scripts/sync-short-titles.mjs writeWhole).
/data/short-titles.json.tmp
/data/short-titles-retry.json.tmp
/data/short-titles-trend.json.tmp

# Pictures the "At a glance" spec writes in CI (tests/question-glance-shots.spec.ts)
/glance-shots/
